# Article dashboard — sentiment panel (server-rendered from Omeka item
# metadata via SentimentExtractor). Strings originate from the retired
# IwacSentiment module so existing installations' translation memory
# keeps working.
msgid "AI sentiment"
msgstr "Sentiment IA"

msgid "Polarity"
msgstr "Polarité"

msgid "Centrality"
msgstr "Centralité"

msgid "Subjectivity"
msgstr "Subjectivité"

msgid "Show reasoning"
msgstr "Voir les justifications"

#. Whether the models landed on the same point of a 1–5 scale
#. (spread 0), one step apart (spread 1), or further (spread 2+).
msgid "Models agree"
msgstr "Les modèles s’accordent"

msgid "Models nearly agree"
msgstr "Les modèles s’accordent presque"

msgid "Models disagree"
msgstr "Les modèles divergent"

#. %s is a comma-separated list of the model names that rated THIS
#. article, composed at render time. The roster changes between
#. annotation campaigns, and a corpus pass in progress means one
#. article may carry three ratings and the next four.
msgid "AI assessments produced independently by %s. Polarity describes the tone towards Islam and Muslims; centrality describes their prominence in the article; subjectivity describes factual or opinion-based language. These ratings need checking against the text. Subjectivity is particularly uncertain, and agreement between models does not establish accuracy."
msgstr "Évaluations produites séparément par %s. La polarité décrit le ton envers l’islam et les musulmans ; la centralité, leur place dans l’article ; la subjectivité, un langage factuel ou fondé sur des opinions. Ces évaluations doivent être confrontées au texte. La subjectivité est particulièrement incertaine et l’accord entre modèles n’établit pas leur exactitude."

